# AP6181 (BCM43362, SDIO id a962): the SlimBOX Wi-Fi HAL (libwifi-hal-common-ext, "multi wifi")
# detects the chip, loads /vendor/lib/modules/dhd.ko with the /vendor/etc/wifi/40181 paths when
# Wi-Fi is turned on and unloads it when Wi-Fi is turned off.
# v1.0 loaded dhd.ko here at boot, like SlimBOX's AP6212 build: the HAL then skipped the chip
# detection, wrote a garbage firmware_path and crashed on every Wi-Fi off (strlen(NULL) in
# is_wifi_driver_loaded); now and then system_server lost the HAL and everything touching Wi-Fi
# (e.g. Settings) hung until a reboot.
on property:wlan.driver.status=ok
    chown root wifi /sys/module/dhd/parameters/firmware_path
    chmod 664 /sys/module/dhd/parameters/firmware_path
